      "sentence": "Preferences-style persistent key/value store backed by AVR EEPROM.",
      "paragraph": "Namespaced key/value storage exposing a Preferences-compatible API subset, so multiplatform sketches can share storage code with ESP32 (native Preferences/NVS) and ESP8266. Log-structured records with CRC-8 integrity and power-loss-safe writes. Keys and namespaces up to 15 chars, values up to 255 bytes. No Arduino String, no thread-safety layer (AVR is single-core).",
